incident_description:
Verizon Travel Charger model A36-502A;
My 11 year old daughter was removing the charger from the wall. The main housing of the charger came off in her hand, leaving a small flat piece in the electrical outlet.  The small piece that was left in the outlet had exposed metal that makes electrical contact to the charger when it's assembled.
My daughter was afraid she would get in trouble for the charger breaking, so she grabbed the small flat piece to remove from the wall socket and was shocked.  She suffered first degree burn on the fingers.
